3. Mutation proof: section 7 catches a CONSISTENT wrong-digest builder
----------------------------------------------------------------------
The byte-exact ESP-config check cannot see a builder that writes the same
wrong digest into both the image and its own idea of the config. Section 7
re-derives the digest from the build-input kernel independently, so it must
fire. Probe (heredoc, python):

    import importlib.util, sys, hashlib
    from pathlib import Path
    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location("vd", "tools/verify-disk.py")
    vd = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec); spec.loader.exec_module(vd)
    LB = Path(".freebuff/ref/limine/limine-binary")
    kernel = Path("kernel/target/x86_64-unknown-none/release/nucleus").read_bytes()
    sidecar = Path("build/limine.conf.nova.hdd").read_bytes()
    want = hashlib.blake2b(kernel, digest_size=64).hexdigest().encode()
    def mk(conf): return vd.Expect(kernel=kernel,
        limine_sys=(LB/"limine-bios.sys").read_bytes(),
        bootx64=(LB/"BOOTX64.EFI").read_bytes(),
        bootia32=(LB/"BOOTIA32.EFI").read_bytes(), conf=conf)
    img = Path("build/nova.hdd").read_bytes()
    fails = vd.verify_image(img, mk(sidecar))
    bad = want[:10] + b"0" + want[11:]
    fails2 = vd.verify_image(img.replace(want, bad), mk(sidecar.replace(want, bad)))

Output (first attempt, probe defect included for honesty):
    baseline failures: 3
    mutated failures: 4 | bootchain section fired: True
      -> bootchain: /NUCLEUS path digest == blake2b-512(build-input kernel) [Limine CONFIG.md lines 435-437]
    MUTATION_PROBE_RC=1
The "baseline 3" was a PROBE bug, not a verifier bug: the first probe fed
one-byte dummy bytes for limine_sys/bootx64/bootia32, so three unrelated
file byte-exact checks failed. Re-run with the real build inputs:

    baseline failures: 0 []
    mutated failures: 1 | bootchain-only: True
      -> bootchain: /NUCLEUS path digest == blake2b-512(build-input kernel) [Limine CONFIG.md lines 435-437]
    MUTATION_PROBE_RC=0

Reading: with a clean baseline, a wrong-but-consistent digest produces
EXACTLY ONE failure — the bootchain digest check. Section 7 is the only
check that can catch this class of builder defect; the byte-exact section
is blind to it by construction.

