5. Addendum — unified sidecar for BOTH images (final design)
------------------------------------------------------------
After sections 1-3 were captured, build-disk.sh was changed so EVERY image
gets a sidecar (the selftest conf has no placeholder, so its sidecar is the
conf verbatim). Verifier behaviour per image, verbatim:

  Regular image (sidecar carries the substituted digest):
    verify-disk: all checks passed        (52 checks incl. both bootchain oks)
  Selftest image (sidecar = conf verbatim, path line has no '#'):
    FAIL   bootchain: kernel path carries no #digest — boot loads an
           unverified kernel [Limine CONFIG.md lines 435-437; acceptable only
           for the dev selftest config]
    verify-disk: 1 check(s) FAILED
  Stale regular sidecar (one nibble flipped), re-tested on the final design:
    stale rc=1
  After rebuilding via scripts/build-disk.sh, the regular image verifies
  clean again (the stale sidecar was the only fault).

The selftest finding is TRUTHFUL, not a regression: check.sh stage 5 runs
only against build/nova.hdd (the regular image), so the suite stays green;
the selftest image's unverified-kernel status is now stated by the verifier
instead of being invisible. check.sh stage 3 builds both images; the sidecar
for each now sits beside it, so no cross-image confusion is possible.
